From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 10:44:51 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] iio: aop_als: report a missing calibration blob once

Without apple/aop-als-cal.bin the probe logs two warnings for one fact,
the firmware loader's

  Direct firmware load for apple/aop-als-cal.bin failed with error -2

and the driver's own "no calibration". The driver's message is the one
that says what the file is for, so request the blob with
request_nowarn().

Correct the comment and the message as well. They say the sensor still
reports without the blob, but the VD6286 of the M4 Pro (J616s) never
sends a report without it: its channel reads ENODATA for the whole boot
and the AOP log shows "Calibration Override:0". Say that the sensor may
not report, so the warning points at the file that is missing.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 6905adadf7079291cb3a063e830633a31513c5cf)
---
 drivers/iio/common/aop_sensors/aop_als.rs | 11 +++++++----
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/iio/common/aop_sensors/aop_als.rs b/drivers/iio/common/aop_sensors/aop_als.rs
index 4cbd1e2846..d41afaba8b 100644
--- a/drivers/iio/common/aop_sensors/aop_als.rs
+++ b/drivers/iio/common/aop_sensors/aop_als.rs
@@ -101,15 +101,18 @@ fn enable_als(
     offset: usize,
 ) -> Result<()> {
     if offset != LUX_OFFSET_CT817 {
-        // The calibration blob comes from macOS and is not installed on every
-        // system. Without it the sensor still reports, uncalibrated.
-        match Firmware::request(c_str!("apple/aop-als-cal.bin"), dev.as_ref()) {
+        // The installer collects the calibration blob from macOS, so it is
+        // not present on every system. Without it the VD6286 of the M4 Pro
+        // never reports and its channel reads ENODATA. The warning below
+        // reports the missing file once, so the firmware loader is asked not
+        // to report it too.
+        match Firmware::request_nowarn(c_str!("apple/aop-als-cal.bin"), dev.as_ref()) {
             Ok(fw) => {
                 set_als_property(aop, svc, ALS_PROP_CALIBRATION, fw.data())?;
             }
             Err(e) => dev_warn!(
                 dev.as_ref(),
-                "no calibration ({:?}); readings are uncalibrated\n",
+                "no apple/aop-als-cal.bin ({:?}); the sensor may not report\n",
                 e
             ),
         }
